# SYNCFB — sync feature branch from `origin/dev`

> **Bootstrap:** Copy to `.cursor/rules/syncfb.mdc` in every DJSharkApps repo. Keep aligned with [`STANDARDS/cloud-agent-handoff.md`](https://github.com/DJSharkApps/djsharkapps-meta/blob/main/STANDARDS/cloud-agent-handoff.md).

Operator says **SYNCFB** / `syncfb` / "sync fb" / "refresh from dev".

## Do

```bash
git fetch origin
git merge origin/dev        # current feature branch
```

Then **report**: commits pulled in · files conflicted · or `already up to date`.
On conflict: resolve, then re-run the repo's gates before any readiness verdict.

## Never

- **Never rebase.** The branch may already be pushed with an open PR; rebase forces a force-push.
- **Never push** as part of SYNCFB — it is a local operation the operator inspects.
- **Never stash** to clean the tree (Park Protocol).
- **Never on `dev` / `beta` / `main`** — feature branches only.

## When to run it

| Moment | Why |
|---|---|
| Cloud Agent — **before executing a parked plan** | The agent writes against current APIs instead of a stale snapshot |
| Local chat — **before `wip-RnP`** | Review / Bugbot / Security must judge the tree that will actually merge |
| Before any ship verb | If `git rev-list --count HEAD..origin/dev` is non-zero |

**Last write wins the review:** a `dev` merge *after* Bugbot or Security invalidates both. Merge first, review second.

## Parked plans — merge code, then re-validate intent

SYNCFB merges code, not intentions. After the merge, before writing code, re-read every file the plan names and report each item as **still valid · already done · renamed / moved · moot**. Do not execute until that report is in.

